---
import PreviewLayout from '../../../layouts/PreviewLayout.astro';

const title = "Hidden Swimming Holes Near Hilo: A Local's Guide | Island Goodes";
const description = "Discover secret swimming holes and freshwater pools near Hilo, Hawaii. Cool off in waterfalls, rivers, and natural pools along the Hamakua Coast.";
const publishDate = "2025-10-25";
---

<PreviewLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="blog-post">
    <header class="post-header">
      <div class="post-header-bg">
        <img src="/images/blog/waterfalls.jpg" alt="Waterfall swimming hole near Hilo" />
      </div>
      <div class="post-header-overlay"></div>
      <div class="post-header-content">
        <nav class="breadcrumb">
          <a href="/preview">Home</a> / <a href="/preview/blog">Blog</a> / Swimming Holes Near Hilo
        </nav>
        <span class="post-category">Nature & Adventure</span>
        <h1>Hidden Swimming Holes Near Hilo</h1>
        <p class="post-tagline">Cool off in nature's pools</p>
        <div class="post-meta">
          <time datetime={publishDate}>October 25, 2025</time>
          <span class="read-time">7 min read</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="post-content">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <p class="lead">
          The Hilo side of the Big Island is blessed with abundant rainfall, which means
          waterfalls, rivers, and natural swimming holes around almost every corner. Here
          are some of our favorite spots to cool off—from easy-access pools to hidden gems
          that take a little more effort to find.
        </p>

        <div class="safety-warning">
          <h3>⚠️ Important Safety Notice</h3>
          <p>
            Rivers and streams along the Hamakua Coast are prone to flash flooding. <strong>Never
            swim if water is surging, murky, or if rain is falling upstream.</strong> Conditions
            can change in minutes. When in doubt, stay out.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2>Swimming Holes to Explore</h2>

        <div class="spot-card">
          <h3>Wai'ale Falls</h3>
          <p class="spot-location">10 minutes from Island Goodes</p>
          <p>
            An easy-to-find swimming hole upstream from Rainbow Falls. The short trail leads
            to a pool with a small waterfall—perfect for a quick dip. It feels rural and
            secluded despite being close to Hilo.
          </p>
          <div class="spot-details">
            <span class="difficulty easy">Easy Access</span>
            <span class="feature">Free</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="spot-card">
          <h3>Waikaumalo Park</h3>
          <p class="spot-location">15 minutes north of Hilo (Old Mamalahoa Hwy)</p>
          <p>
            A local favorite that doesn't appear in most guidebooks. Deep pools perfect for
            jumping, surrounded by lush vegetation. The water is cool and refreshing—exactly
            what you need on a humid Hilo day.
          </p>
          <div class="spot-details">
            <span class="difficulty easy">Easy Access</span>
            <span class="feature">Hidden Gem</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="spot-card">
          <h3>6 Tons Swimming Hole</h3>
          <p class="spot-location">Old Mamalahoa Highway at Kawainui Stream</p>
          <p>
            Named for the old weight limit on the bridge, this spot features a small waterfall
            cascading into a refreshing pool. It's right off the scenic Old Mamalahoa Highway,
            making it easy to combine with a drive up the Hamakua Coast.
          </p>
          <div class="spot-details">
            <span class="difficulty easy">Roadside Access</span>
            <span class="feature">Waterfall</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="spot-card featured">
          <span class="spot-badge">Worth the Trip</span>
          <h3>Kulaniapia Falls</h3>
          <p class="spot-location">Outskirts of Hilo (private property)</p>
          <p>
            A stunning 120-foot private waterfall with a swimming pool at its base. While
            it's on the grounds of a boutique inn, day passes are available for visitors
            who aren't staying there. It's worth the fee for this magical setting.
          </p>
          <div class="spot-details">
            <span class="difficulty easy">Easy (day pass required)</span>
            <span class="feature">120ft Waterfall</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="spot-card">
          <h3>Umauma Falls</h3>
          <p class="spot-location">16 miles north of Hilo</p>
          <p>
            Three-tiered waterfall on private property with swimming, kayaking, and zipline
            options. The $10 access fee includes beautiful gardens and multiple viewpoints.
            A great half-day adventure.
          </p>
          <div class="spot-details">
            <span class="difficulty easy">$10 Access Fee</span>
            <span class="feature">3-Tier Falls</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="spot-card">
          <h3>Hilo Hot Ponds (Ahalanui)</h3>
          <p class="spot-location">Puna District (45 min from Hilo)</p>
          <p>
            Naturally heated thermal pools right by the ocean, warmed to about 90°F by
            volcanic activity. The mineral-rich water is said to have therapeutic benefits.
            Locals come here to soak and relax.
          </p>
          <div class="spot-details">
            <span class="difficulty easy">Easy Access</span>
            <span class="feature">Thermal Springs</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>Where NOT to Swim</h2>
        <div class="warning-box">
          <h4>Rainbow Falls</h4>
          <p>Viewing only! Despite its beauty, the currents below Rainbow Falls are treacherous. This is a photography spot, not a swimming hole.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="warning-box">
          <h4>Boiling Pots (Pe'epe'e Falls)</h4>
          <p>Absolutely no swimming. Multiple drownings have occurred here due to deceptive currents and underwater caves. Viewing only from the overlook.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>What to Bring</h2>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Water shoes - rocks can be slippery</li>
          <li>Towel and change of clothes</li>
          <li>Reef-safe sunscreen</li>
          <li>Drinking water and snacks</li>
          <li>Waterproof bag for valuables</li>
          <li>Bug spray for trailside spots</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Best Time to Visit</h2>
        <p>
          Morning is generally best—calmer water, fewer people, and you can check conditions
          before committing. After heavy rain, wait at least 24 hours before swimming in any
          river or stream. The water needs time to clear and levels need to drop.
        </p>

        <div class="cta-box">
          <h3>Your Hilo Adventure Awaits</h3>
          <p>
            Stay at Island Goodes and explore the hidden swimming holes of the Hamakua Coast.
            We're happy to share our favorite spots and current conditions.
          </p>
          <a href="https://v2.reservationkey.com/3655/reserve/c" class="btn btn-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book Your Stay</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</PreviewLayout>

<style>
  .post-header { position: relative; min-height: 50vh; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; text-align: center; color: #fff; padding: 10rem 2rem 4rem; }
  .post-header-bg { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: -2; }
  .post-header-bg img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  .post-header-overlay { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: -1; background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(0,0,0,0.3) 0%, rgba(0,0,0,0.7) 100%); }
  .post-header-content { max-width: 800px; }
  .post-category { display: inline-block; background: var(--color-secondary); color: #1a1a1a; padding: 0.375rem 1rem; border-radius: 50px; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .post-header h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .post-tagline { font-size: 1.25rem; opacity: 0.9; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .post-meta { display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; justify-content: center; opacity: 0.9; font-size: 0.9375rem; }

  .post-content { padding: var(--section-padding) 0; }
  .container.narrow { max-width: 750px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 2rem; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--color-text-light); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem; }

  .post-content h2 { color: var(--color-text); font-size: 1.75rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; }
  .post-content p { color: var(--color-text-light); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }

  .safety-warning { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #b43c3c 0%, #8b2d2d 100%); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; color: #fff; margin: 2rem 0; }
  .safety-warning h3 { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .safety-warning p { margin: 0; opacity: 0.95; }

  .spot-card { background: #fff; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 16px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.06); position: relative; }
  .spot-card.featured { border: 2px solid var(--color-secondary); }
  .spot-badge { position: absolute; top: -0.75rem; right: 1.5rem; background: var(--color-secondary); color: #1a1a1a; padding: 0.375rem 1rem; border-radius: 50px; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .spot-card h3 { color: var(--color-text); font-size: 1.375rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
  .spot-location { color: var(--color-primary); font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 1rem !important; }
  .spot-card > p:not(.spot-location) { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .spot-details { display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .difficulty, .feature { display: inline-block; padding: 0.375rem 0.875rem; border-radius: 50px; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .difficulty.easy { background: rgba(27, 107, 90, 0.1); color: var(--color-primary); }
  .feature { background: var(--color-bg-alt); color: var(--color-text-light); }

  .warning-box { background: rgba(180, 60, 60, 0.08); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 12px; margin-bottom: 1rem; border-left: 4px solid #b43c3c; }
  .warning-box h4 { color: #b43c3c; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem; }
  .warning-box p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--color-text-light); }

  .checklist { list-style: none; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
  .checklist li { padding: 0.5rem 0; padding-left: 1.75rem; position: relative; color: var(--color-text-light); }
  .checklist li::before { content: "✓"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--color-primary); font-weight: 600; }

  .cta-box { background: var(--gradient-primary); padding: 2.5rem; border-radius: 16px; text-align: center; color: #fff; margin-top: 3rem; }
  .cta-box h3 { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .cta-box p { opacity: 0.9; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
</style>
